ype":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve the packet. The change is a narrow, conservative refactor and the scope problem that caused the last rejection is fixed.\n\n**Scope (rule R2):** In `external/sdkjs`, the diff from `refs/theseus/base` to HEAD now touches only 4 target files (+101/−1). The `.theseus-addons` gitlink from commit bf9b2ea is removed in b152f87, and `git status` in that clone is clean. The budget is met: 4 code files out of 6 allowed, about 100 lines out of 800.\n\n**Goal and contract:**\n- The full font walk now runs only for remote applies that touch something other than text. When a remote apply touches only `CDocumentContentElementBase` objects (paragraph, table, block-level content control) or `CRun` objects, fonts are collected from just those objects plus the theme fonts. Any other class, or a change with no class, falls back to the full `CheckFontNeeds`.\n- The font list is only ever extended and never shrinks. Only fonts used by the touched objects can be new: style, numbering and theme changes force the full walk. So the \"no missing glyphs\" rule in `contract.preserve` holds.\n- Opening, saving and image paths, and any apply before the document has finished loading, keep the full walk.\n- Getting the change classes from `CoHistory` between `m_nRecalcIndexStart` and `m_nRecalcIndexEnd` is correct. The packet context wrongly said `m_aChanges` carries `.Class`; the executor caught this and logged it as a surprise.\n\n**Minor points that don't block approval:**\n- The pending classes are consumed by the next `pre_Save`, whichever path calls it. A save or image `pre_Save` that runs between an apply and its own `pre_Save` would take the incremental path. That is still safe because the list only grows.\n- No new tests cover `GetFontNamesFromClasses` or the fallback logic. For a refactor that keeps behaviour, the existing suites (unit tests plus 6195 sdkjs-word assertions) are acceptable.\n- The executor saw one failed run of `unit.sh` (2 failed, 176 passed) and didn't find out which tests failed. The factory's run on this commit passed, but that test flakiness should be tracked.\n\n**Not done here:** The goal's before/after profile on the 100-page docx, and a browser check of a remote change, were not done in this packet. They are handed off to PKT-0071, which is listed under Spawned packets and sits in the pending queue. The Executor log, Lessons for the Atlas and friction lines are all filled in.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Scope fixed (only the 4 target files); remote applies touching only text use the incremental path, anything else gets the full walk; profiling handed to PKT-0071","ttft_ms":2438,"type":"result","duration_ms":26224,"uuid":"cd5d4511-b6b1-477c-a5d0-0913229e6108","ttft_stream_ms":986,"time_to_request_ms":408,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":293,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":17,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":20,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":4,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":31,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":163,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":228,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":258,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1040,"process_wall_ms_turn":26223,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":490,"process_wall_ms_streaming":22799,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":300,"main_stream_chunk_count":116,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":6,"cpu_ms":18,"major_